+        <div class="transport">
+          <div class="buttons"><button id="play" class="primary" type="button">▶ Play</button><button id="step" type="button">Step +0.25 s</button><button id="reset" type="button">↺ Reset</button><button id="finish" type="button">To end ↗</button></div>
+          <div class="clock"><span id="time">00.00</span><span> / 60 s</span></div>
+        </div>
+        <label class="scrubber" for="scrub"><span>Inspect mission time</span><input id="scrub" type="range" min="0" max="240" step="1" value="0"><output id="scrub-value" for="scrub">0.00 s</output></label>
+        <div class="telemetry" aria-label="Current mission telemetry" aria-live="off">
+          <div><span>TRUE DEPTH</span><strong id="truth-value">8.00 <small>m</small></strong></div>
+          <div><span>ESTIMATE B</span><strong id="estimate-value">8.00 <small>m</small></strong></div>
+          <div><span>95% HALF-WIDTH</span><strong id="width-value">1.96 <small>m</small></strong></div>
+          <div><span>ACTUAL ERROR |B|</span><strong id="error-value">0.00 <small>m</small></strong></div>
+        </div>
+        <p id="scene-text" class="scene-text"></p>
+      </section>
+      <aside class="settings panel" aria-labelledby="settings-title">
+        <div class="panel-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / EXPERIMENT DESK</p><h2 id="settings-title">Reality ≠ belief</h2></div><span class="mini-mark">⌁</span></div>
+        <fieldset><legend>The actual world</legend><p class="hint">Changes create a new mission at t = 0.</p>
+          <label for="sigma">Sensor noise <span>σ / m</span></label><div class="value-line"><output id="sigma-value" for="sigma">0.80</output><span>standard deviation</span></div><input id="sigma" type="range" min="0.05" max="2" step="0.05" value="0.8"><p class="hint" id="actual-variance">Actual variance: 0.64 m²</p>
+          <label for="seed">Replay seed</label><div class="seed-row"><input id="seed" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" step="1" value="42"><button id="replay" type="button">Replay</button></div>
+        </fieldset>
+        <fieldset class="belief"><legend>What filter B assumes</legend><p class="hint">Retune instantly on the same recorded data.</p>
+          <label for="r">Measurement variance <span>R / m²</span></label><div class="value-line"><output id="r-value" for="r">0.64</output><span>trust the fix less →</span></div><input id="r" type="range" min="0.01" max="9" step="0.01" value="0.64">
+          <label for="q">Acceleration variance <span>q / m²/s⁴</span></label><div class="value-line"><output id="q-value" for="q">0.0036</output><span>trust the model less →</span></div><input id="q" type="range" min="0" max="0.06" step="0.0004" value="0.0036"><p class="hint">Q = q GGᵀ, G = [h²/2, h]ᵀ.<br>Actual acceleration σ = 0.06 m/s².</p>
+          <div class="tuning-actions"><button id="pin" type="button">Pin B as reference A</button><button id="match" type="button">Match actual noise</button></div>
+          <p class="pin-note" id="pin-note">A pinned: R 0.64 · q 0.0036</p>
+        </fieldset>
+        <div class="desk-note"><span class="small-number">TRY THIS / 01</span><p>Pin a baseline. Increase R. Does the filter follow each fix as closely?</p><p class="hint">Every fix is identical for A and B. Only their assumptions differ.</p></div>
+      </aside>
+    </div>
+    <section class="results panel" aria-labelledby="results-title">
+      <div class="panel-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / PAIRED OBSERVATIONS</p><h2 id="results-title">Same ocean. Two beliefs.</h2></div><span id="result-stage" class="tag">CUMULATIVE · 0 s</span></div>
+      <div class="results-layout"><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Depth RMSE up to the inspected time, in meters. Lower means less error.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Estimator</th><th scope="col">RMSE / m</th><th scope="col">Truth in 95% band</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="b-row"><th scope="row">B / active filter</th><td id="rmse-b">—</td><td id="coverage-b">—</td></tr><tr class="a-row"><th scope="row">A / pinned filter</th><td id="rmse-a">—</td><td id="coverage-a">—</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Raw depth fixes</th><td id="rmse-raw">—</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Dead reckoning</th><td id="rmse-dead">—</td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="hint" id="metric-note">Filter and dead reckoning use every 0.25 s step. Raw RMSE uses available fixes only.</p></div>
+      <div class="diagnosis"><p class="eyebrow">FIELD DIAGNOSIS</p><h3 id="diagnosis-title">Ready for descent.</h3><p id="diagnosis-text">Press Play, step one prediction, or go straight to the mission summary.</p><div class="status-line"><span id="fix-status">Initial state</span><span id="fix-count">0 fixes</span></div></div></div>
+      <p id="summary" class="summary" hidden></p>
+    </section>
+    <section id="learn" class="learning" aria-labelledby="learn-title">
+      <div class="lesson-intro"><p class="eyebrow">04 / INSIDE THE FILTER</p><h2 id="learn-title">Predict.<br>Listen.<br><em>Correct.</em></h2><p>The robot has a depth and a vertical velocity. Thrust advances its prediction. A processed depth fix pulls the estimate toward the sensor, weighted by uncertainty.</p><p>Truth is visible to you for scoring. The filter never sees it.</p><label for="question">Before a dropout, predict what will happen to the band.</label><select id="question"><option value="">Choose your prediction…</option><option value="grows">It will grow without new fixes</option><option value="shrinks">It will shrink as time passes</option><option value="same">It will stay the same</option></select><p id="answer" class="answer" aria-live="polite"></p></div>
+      <div class="lesson-card panel"><div class="panel-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">WORKED EXAMPLE / YOUR CURRENT STEP</p><h3 id="worked-title">A prior before the first fix</h3></div></div>
+        <ol class="worked"><li><span class="step-number">1</span><div><h4>Predict with thrust</h4><code>p⁻ = p + hv + ½h²u<br>v⁻ = v + hu<br>P⁻ = FPFᵀ + Q</code><p id="predict-text"></p></div></li><li><span class="step-number">2</span><div><h4>Compare the fix</h4><code>innovation = z − p⁻<br>K = P⁻Hᵀ / (P⁻₀₀ + R)</code><p id="innovation-text"></p></div></li><li><span class="step-number">3</span><div><h4>Correct the estimate</h4><code>x = x⁻ + K · innovation</code><p id="correct-text"></p></div></li></ol>
+        <p class="hint">Step advances 0.25 s; fixes arrive every 1 s. Covariance uses the Joseph update: P = (I−KH)P⁻(I−KH)ᵀ + KRKᵀ.</p>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+    <details class="model panel"><summary>Model, units &amp; limits <span>+</span></summary><div class="model-body"><p>This is a linear, one-dimensional depth experiment, positive downward. h = 0.25 s, state x = [depth in m, velocity in m/s], F = [[1,h],[0,1]], H = [1,0]. Known thrust acceleration u is applied to both world and model. Initial x = [8, 0.12], P = diag(1 m², 0.04 m²/s²).</p><p>Every step draws an independent acceleration disturbance with standard deviation 0.06 m/s², constant over that interval. Q = q [[h⁴/4,h³/2],[h³/2,h²]]. q is acceleration variance, not a standard deviation or continuous-time spectral density. The sensor slider is actual standard deviation σ; filter R is assumed variance. Nominal matched values are q = 0.0036 and R = σ².</p><p>The crosses are simulated, processed localization depth fixes every second. They are not raw sonar ranges, bearings, underwater GPS, or DVL readings. No DVL is modeled. Dead reckoning integrates only the commanded acceleration. Fix noise is independent Gaussian noise. Current and bias deliberately break the filter's assumptions; this model cannot estimate persistent bias or ocean dynamics.</p><p>The mint band is the marginal Gaussian depth interval p̂ ± 1.96√P₀₀, about 95% under a correct model. It is not a two-dimensional confidence ellipse or a guarantee. Empirical coverage can differ, especially during faults. RMSE compares positions to simulation truth and does not claim that filtering always improves accuracy.</p><p>RoboSub-inspired exploration, with gate / slalom / bin navigation as inspiration. This depth transect is a simplified teaching exercise, not an official course or scoring system.</p><p class="sources">Read further: <a href="https://www.cs.unc.edu/~welch/media/pdf/kalman_intro.pdf">Welch &amp; Bishop’s introduction</a> · <a href="https://www.bzarg.com/p/how-a-kalman-filter-works-in-pictures/">A visual filter explanation</a> · <a href="https://robonation.gitbook.io/robosub-resources/section-3-autonomy-challenge/3.2-task-descriptions">RoboSub task descriptions</a> · <a href="https://robosub.org/programs/2026/">RoboSub 2026</a></p></div></details>
+  </main>
+  <footer><span>ABYSS / A SMALL WINDOW INTO UNCERTAINTY</span><span>Local simulation · no uploads · no dependencies</span><a href="../secret/">Back to Secret ↗</a></footer>
+  <p id="announcement" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
+</body>
+</html>

changes.diff:
(function () {
  'use strict';
  const E = window.Abyss, $ = id => document.getElementById(id);
  const world = { seed: 42, sigma: 0.8, scenario: 'nominal' };
  let tuning = { ...E.DEFAULT }, pinned = { ...E.DEFAULT };
  let data, b, a, cursor = 0, timer = null;
  const fmt = (v, n = 2) => v === null || !Number.isFinite(v) ? '—' : v.toFixed(n);
  const announce = message => { $('announcement').textContent = message; };
  const svg = (tag, attrs) => {
    const element = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', tag);
    Object.entries(attrs).forEach(([key, value]) => element.setAttribute(key, value));
    return element;
  };
  function pause() { if (timer !== null) clearInterval(timer); timer = null; }
  function compute() { b = E.run(data, tuning); a = E.run(data, pinned); }
  function fresh() { pause(); cursor = 0; data = E.generate(world); compute(); render(); }
  function readSeed() {
    const input = $('seed');
    if (!input.checkValidity() || input.value === '') { input.reportValidity(); return false; }
    world.seed = Number(input.value); return true;
  }
  function setTuning() {
    tuning = { q: Number($('q').value), r: Number($('r').value) };
    compute(); render();
  }
  function step() {
    if (cursor >= data.length - 1) return;
    cursor++;
    if (cursor === data.length - 1) { pause(); announce('Mission complete. Read the paired observations and mission summary.'); }
    render();
  }
  function togglePlay() {
    if (timer !== null) { pause(); render(); announce('Mission paused.'); return; }
    if (cursor >= data.length - 1) cursor = 0;
    timer = setInterval(step, 125); // Fixed simulated dt, independent of browser wall-clock jitter.
    render(); announce('Mission playing at twice real time.');
  }
  function plot() {
    // Fixed mission-wide scale keeps the instrument stable when scrubbing or retuning.
    const minDepth = Math.min(0, ...b.map(f => f.x[0] - f.width), ...a.map(f => f.x[0]), ...data.filter(f => f.z !== null).map(f => f.z));
    const maxDepth = Math.max(18, ...b.map(f => f.x[0] + f.width), ...a.map(f => f.x[0]), ...data.map(f => f.truth[0]), ...data.filter(f => f.z !== null).map(f => f.z), ...b.map(f => f.dead[0]));
    const lo = Math.floor(minDepth / 2) * 2, hi = Math.ceil(maxDepth / 2) * 2;
    const x = t => 65 + t / E.DURATION * 740, y = d => 38 + (d - lo) / (hi - lo) * 250;
    const grid = $('grid'); grid.replaceChildren();
    for (let i = 0; i <= 4; i++) {
      const depth = lo + (hi - lo) * i / 4, py = y(depth);
      grid.append(svg('line', { x1: 65, x2: 805, y1: py, y2: py, class: 'grid-line' }));
      const label = svg('text', { x: 49, y: py + 3, 'text-anchor': 'end', class: 'grid-label' }); label.textContent = fmt(depth, 0); grid.append(label);
    }
    for (let t = 0; t <= 60; t += 10) {
      grid.append(svg('line', { x1: x(t), x2: x(t), y1: 38, y2: 288, class: 'grid-line' }));
      const label = svg('text', { x: x(t), y: 309, 'text-anchor': 'middle', class: 'grid-label' }); label.textContent = t; grid.append(label);
    }
    const fault = $('fault-region'); fault.replaceChildren();
    if (world.scenario !== 'nominal') {
      const from = world.scenario === 'current' ? 18 : 20, to = world.scenario === 'dropout' ? 36 : world.scenario === 'current' ? 38 : 60;
      fault.append(svg('rect', { x: x(from), y: 38, width: x(to) - x(from), height: 250, fill: '#f7bf7b', opacity: '.045' }));
      const label = svg('text', { x: x(from) + 6, y: 31, fill: '#f7bf7b', 'font-size': 10, 'font-family': 'monospace' }); label.textContent = world.scenario === 'dropout' ? 'NO FIXES / 20–36 s' : world.scenario === 'current' ? 'CURRENT / 18–38 s' : 'BIAS / +1.8 m'; fault.append(label);
    }
    const history = b.slice(0, cursor + 1);
    const path = (frames, value) => frames.map((f, i) => `${i ? 'L' : 'M'}${fmt(x(f.t))},${fmt(y(value(f)))}`).join(' ');
    $('truth-path').setAttribute('d', path(history, f => f.truth[0]));
    $('filter-path').setAttribute('d', path(history, f => f.x[0]));
    $('dead-path').setAttribute('d', path(history, f => f.dead[0]));
    $('a-path').setAttribute('d', path(a.slice(0, cursor + 1), f => f.x[0]));
    $('band').setAttribute('d', path(history, f => f.x[0] - f.width) + history.slice().reverse().map(f => `L${fmt(x(f.t))},${fmt(y(f.x[0] + f.width))}`).join(' ') + 'Z');
    const fixes = $('fixes'); fixes.replaceChildren();
    history.filter(f => f.z !== null).forEach(f => {
      const px = x(f.t), py = y(f.z);
      fixes.append(svg('path', { d: `M${px - 3},${py - 3}l6,6m-6,0l6,-6` }));
    });
    const f = b[cursor], px = x(f.t), py = y(f.x[0]);
    $('robot').setAttribute('transform', `translate(${px},${py})`);
    $('truth-dot').setAttribute('transform', `translate(${px},${y(f.truth[0])})`);
    $('robot-label').setAttribute('x', Math.min(px + 22, 725));
    $('robot-label').setAttribute('y', py - 22);
    $('cursor-line').setAttribute('x1', px); $('cursor-line').setAttribute('x2', px);
  }
  function render() {
    const f = b[cursor], ref = a[cursor], m = f.metrics, done = cursor === data.length - 1;
    $('state').textContent = done ? 'COMPLETE' : timer !== null ? 'RUNNING' : cursor ? 'PAUSED' : 'READY';
    $('play').textContent = timer !== null ? 'Ⅱ Pause' : done ? '▶ Play again' : '▶ Play';
    $('step').disabled = done; $('finish').disabled = done;
    $('time').textContent = f.t.toFixed(2).padStart(5, '0'); $('scrub').value = cursor; $('scrub-value').textContent = `${fmt(f.t)} s`;
    $('sigma-value').value = fmt(world.sigma); $('r-value').value = fmt(tuning.r); $('q-value').value = fmt(tuning.q, 4);
    $('actual-variance').textContent = `Actual variance: ${fmt(world.sigma ** 2)} m²`;
    $('pin-note').textContent = `A pinned: R ${fmt(pinned.r)} · q ${fmt(pinned.q, 4)}`;
    $('scenario-note').textContent = E.SCENARIOS[world.scenario].note;
    for (const [id, v] of [['truth-value', f.truth[0]], ['estimate-value', f.x[0]], ['width-value', f.width], ['error-value', Math.abs(f.error)]]) $(id).innerHTML = `${fmt(v)} <small>m</small>`;
    $('scene-text').textContent = `At ${fmt(f.t)} s: velocity B ${fmt(f.x[1], 3)} m/s; depth fix ${f.z === null ? 'unavailable at this step' : fmt(f.z) + ' m'}; depth interval [${fmt(f.x[0] - f.width)}, ${fmt(f.x[0] + f.width)}] m. ${Math.abs(f.error) <= f.width ? 'Truth is inside' : 'Truth is outside'} the band.`;
    $('result-stage').textContent = `${done ? 'MISSION COMPLETE' : 'CUMULATIVE'} · ${fmt(f.t, 1)} s`;
    $('rmse-b').textContent = fmt(m.filter, 3); $('rmse-a').textContent = fmt(ref.metrics.filter, 3);
    $('rmse-raw').textContent = fmt(m.raw, 3); $('rmse-dead').textContent = fmt(m.dead, 3);
    $('coverage-b').textContent = m.coverage === null ? '—' : fmt(m.coverage, 1) + '%';
    $('coverage-a').textContent = ref.metrics.coverage === null ? '—' : fmt(ref.metrics.coverage, 1) + '%';
    $('fix-status').textContent = f.event; $('fix-count').textContent = `${m.rawCount} fixes`;
    $('metric-note').textContent = `Filter and dead reckoning: ${cursor} steps. Raw RMSE: ${m.rawCount} available fixes. A and B use identical commands and fixes.`;
    let title = 'Ready for descent.', text = 'Press Play, step one prediction, or go straight to the mission summary. Pin B, change R, and compare.';
    if (cursor) {
      if (world.scenario === 'dropout' && f.t >= 20 && f.t < 36) { title = 'Listening to silence.'; text = `No fixes: the robot can only predict. The 95% half-width is ${fmt(f.width)} m. Inspect 19 s, then 35 s to see how uncertainty accumulates.`; }
      else if (world.scenario === 'bias' && f.t >= 20) { title = 'Confident can be wrong.'; text = `The sensor now reads 1.8 m too deep. B's actual error is ${fmt(Math.abs(f.error))} m while its half-width is ${fmt(f.width)} m. A filter without a bias state cannot distinguish bias from motion.`; }
      else if (world.scenario === 'current' && f.t >= 18) { title = 'The ocean changed the model.'; text = `Unmodeled downward acceleration pushes truth away from dead reckoning. Larger q lets the filter adapt faster, but usually gives noisier estimates and wider intervals.`; }
      else if (done && world.scenario === 'dropout') { title = 'Contact restored. Belief repaired.'; text = 'At 36 s, depth fixes resume and the band contracts. The score includes the blind interval; the final narrow band does not erase earlier error.'; }
      else { title = done ? 'A quieter estimate, measured.' : f.z === null ? 'Predict now. Correct at the next fix.' : 'A fix pulls the estimate.'; text = f.z === null ? 'Between one-second depth fixes, the filter advances using known thrust and velocity. Uncertainty propagates even while no measurement arrives.' : `The depth gain is ${fmt(f.K[0], 3)}: B applies ${(100 * f.K[0]).toFixed(1)}% of the innovation. Raising R generally weakens that correction. Lower RMSE and calibrated uncertainty are different goals.`; }
    }
    $('diagnosis-title').textContent = title; $('diagnosis-text').textContent = text;
    $('summary').hidden = !done;
    $('summary').textContent = `60 s mission complete · seed ${world.seed} · ${E.SCENARIOS[world.scenario].title}. B RMSE ${fmt(m.filter, 3)} m; A ${fmt(ref.metrics.filter, 3)} m; raw fixes ${fmt(m.raw, 3)} m; dead reckoning ${fmt(m.dead, 3)} m. B's 95% band covered truth on ${fmt(m.coverage, 1)}% of steps. ${m.filter < ref.metrics.filter ? 'B reduced error relative to A for this run.' : m.filter > ref.metrics.filter ? 'A had less error than B for this run.' : 'A and B have equal error with the same tuning.'} Replay another seed before generalizing.`;
    $('worked-title').textContent = `t = ${fmt(f.t)} s · ${cursor ? f.z === null ? 'prediction only' : 'predict + correct' : 'initial prior'}`;
    $('predict-text').textContent = cursor ? `h = 0.25 s, u = ${fmt(f.u, 3)} m/s² → predicted depth ${fmt(f.prior.x[0], 3)} m, velocity ${fmt(f.prior.x[1], 3)} m/s. Prior depth variance ${fmt(f.prior.P[0][0], 4)} m².` : 'Begin at depth 8.000 m, velocity 0.120 m/s. Initial depth variance is 1.0000 m². Step four times to see the first sensor correction.';
    $('innovation-text').textContent = f.z === null ? 'No fix at this step: there is no innovation or correction gain to apply.' : `z = ${fmt(f.z, 3)} m; z − p⁻ = ${fmt(f.innovation, 3)} m. R = ${fmt(tuning.r)} m². K = [${fmt(f.K[0], 3)}, ${fmt(f.K[1], 3)} s⁻¹].`;
    $('correct-text').textContent = f.z === null ? `Keep the predicted state. Depth variance ${fmt(f.P[0][0], 4)} m²; interval half-width ${fmt(f.width, 3)} m.` : `p = ${fmt(f.prior.x[0], 3)} + ${fmt(f.K[0], 3)} × ${fmt(f.innovation, 3)} = ${fmt(f.x[0], 3)} m. Velocity becomes ${fmt(f.x[1], 3)} m/s. Depth variance contracts to ${fmt(f.P[0][0], 4)} m².`;
    plot();
  }
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-scenario]').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
    world.scenario = button.dataset.scenario;
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-scenario]').forEach(item => item.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(item === button)));
    fresh(); announce(`${E.SCENARIOS[world.scenario].title}. Mission reset.`);
  }));
  $('play').addEventListener('click', togglePlay);
  $('step').addEventListener('click', () => { pause(); step(); announce(`Stepped to ${fmt(b[cursor].t)} seconds. ${b[cursor].event}.`); });
  $('reset').addEventListener('click', () => { pause(); cursor = 0; render(); announce('Mission reset with identical data and tuning.'); });
  $('finish').addEventListener('click', () => { pause(); cursor = data.length - 1; render(); announce('Mission complete. Read the summary below.'); });
  $('scrub').addEventListener('input', () => { pause(); cursor = Number($('scrub').value); render(); });
  $('sigma').addEventListener('input', () => { world.sigma = Number($('sigma').value); fresh(); });
  $('sigma').addEventListener('change', () => announce('Actual noise changed. New mission ready.'));
  $('replay').addEventListener('click', () => { if (readSeed()) { fresh(); announce(`Replay ready with seed ${world.seed}.`); } });
  $('seed').addEventListener('keydown', event => { if (event.key === 'Enter' && readSeed()) { fresh(); announce(`Replay ready with seed ${world.seed}.`); } });
  ['q', 'r'].forEach(id => $(id).addEventListener('input', setTuning));
  $('pin').addEventListener('click', () => { pinned = { ...tuning }; compute(); render(); announce('Current tuning pinned as filter A. Change B to compare.'); });
  $('match').addEventListener('click', () => { $('q').value = E.DEFAULT.q; $('r').value = world.sigma ** 2; setTuning(); announce('B now matches actual nominal noise. Fault scenarios still violate the model.'); });
  $('question').addEventListener('change', () => { const value = $('question').value; $('answer').textContent = value ? value === 'grows' ? 'Yes. With no fixes, position uncertainty accumulates from velocity uncertainty and Q. Try Dropout and inspect 19 s versus 35 s.' : 'Look at P⁻ = FPFᵀ + Q: velocity uncertainty and new disturbances accumulate. The depth band grows. Try the Dropout scenario.' : ''; });
  document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => { if (document.hidden && timer !== null) { pause(); render(); } });
  fresh();
})();

