+# Abyss — uncertainty observatory
+
+Completed independently in the assigned `workbench` working copy. No rival implementation or report was inspected. No sub-agents, commits, publication, or shared infrastructure changes were used.
+
+## Setup and preview
+
+No install, build, backend, external font, or CDN is needed for the activity. From this working copy:
+
+```powershell
+node kalman/preview.cjs
+```
+
+Open **http://localhost:8313/secret/** and select the fourth project, **Abyss**, or open **http://localhost:8313/kalman/** directly. The preview started successfully on port 8313 during verification; reuse it if still running. Ctrl+C stops a foreground preview. This optional server serves static files. Private-upload operations require the existing Worker or its separate in-memory preview.
+
+## Finished activity
+
+- Custom underwater SVG instrument with distinct trace shapes: white truth, orange cross-shaped processed depth fixes, mint estimate B, violet dotted reference A, gray dashed dead reckoning. B's shaded band is p̂ ± 1.96√P₀₀. A robot marks estimated depth. Horizontal position in the scene represents mission time, not horizontal travel.
+- Play/pause, 0.25 s step, deterministic reset, time scrubber, replay seed, and a 60 s endpoint with summary. Starts paused. Playback is 2× real time and pauses when the tab becomes hidden.
+- Quiet-water, dropout, unmodeled-current, and biased-sensor presets with plot fault windows and explanations. Dropout removes fixes from 20–36 s. Current adds downward acceleration. Bias adds 1.8 m to fixes after 20 s.
+- Actual sensor standard deviation is separate from assumed R and acceleration variance q. Actual disturbance σ is fixed at 0.06 m/s². Match sets R=σ² and q=0.0036, including the lowest sensor setting.
+- Pin B as A, then retune B on identical commands and fixes. Retuning reprocesses the recorded history while retaining the timestamp; it does not simulate a firmware change mid-mission. World changes restart both filters on a common new dataset.
+- Live depth, velocity, fix, error, interval bounds, RMSE for raw fixes/filter/dead reckoning, empirical band coverage, and fix count. Filter/dead-reckoning metrics use all post-initial steps; raw RMSE uses available fixes.
+- Worked predict/correct example with actual current-step values, learner prediction and feedback, expandable model/units/limits and sources. Truth is used only for display and scoring.
+- Native keyboard controls, visible focus, ≥44 px controls, skip link, phone-specific plot coordinates, semantic numerical plot equivalent, silent numeric outputs, action-level announcements, reduced-motion CSS, and no-JavaScript explanation.
+- Fourth Secret card and four-project footer using the existing accessible descriptions and safe new-tab convention.
+
+## Actual numerical and regression verification
+
+`node --test tests/*.test.cjs` — **30 passed, 0 failed**: the 20 existing navigation/Worker/private-upload tests plus 10 new checks. Output: `work/verification/abyss/test-results.txt`.
+
+Verified the exact fixture h=1,u=0,Q=0,R=1,x=[0,0],P=I,z=3 → x=[2,1],K=[2/3,1/3],P=[[2/3,1/3],[1/3,2/3]]. Verified known-control prediction, Q=qGGᵀ, Joseph covariance correction, prediction-only dropout, growing uncertainty and reacquisition contraction, deterministic replay, measurement-stream independence from tuning, and truth independence of states/gains/covariance. Dataset mutation is checked. Fault timing and independently summed RMSE agree with results.
+
+Covariance remains finite, symmetric and PSD through **100,000 steps**, including long dropout intervals. All scenarios pass tuning boundaries including q=0 and R=0.0001/0.0025/9. The finite endpoint is verified. All portfolio local script/style references resolve, with the viewer checked at its actual Worker route `/uploads/{id}/`. Existing Worker upload/download/session/deletion/legacy regressions pass.
+
+Seed **42**, σ=**0.8 m**, q=**0.0036 m²/s⁴**, R=**0.64 m²**, at 60 s:
+
+| Scenario | Filter RMSE / m | Raw RMSE / m | Dead reckoning RMSE / m | Band coverage | Fixes |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| Quiet water | 0.367133 | 0.816008 | 4.319518 | 100.00% | 60 |
+| Dropout | 0.572999 | 0.866269 | 4.319518 | 100.00% | 44 |
+| Current | 0.538609 | 0.816008 | 11.081575 | 86.67% | 60 |
+| Sensor bias | 1.427203 | 1.609461 | 4.319518 | 36.25% | 60 |
+
+These are actual seeded results, not user studies or general improvement guarantees. Coverage counts the 240 post-initial steps; a single run need not attain exactly 95%.
+
+Passed `node --check kalman/engine.js`, `node --check kalman/app.js`, and `node --check kalman/preview.cjs`. Running the tests also parses both changed test files. `git diff --check` passed with only usual LF-to-CRLF notices. A separate trailing-whitespace scan covers new untracked deliverables.
+
+## Actual browser verification
+
+Used **Edge** through the Browser skill. Viewport overrides were restored afterward.
+
+| Viewport | Result |
+|---|---|
+| 1440×900 | Desktop visually inspected; no overflow; all controls ≥44 px |
+| 390×844 | Phone visually inspected; client and scroll widths both 375 px; compact plot; all controls ≥44 px |
+| 320×740 | Narrow phone visually inspected; client and scroll widths both 305 px; compact plot; all controls ≥44 px |
+
+The 15 px difference is the browser scrollbar. Evidence is in `work/verification/abyss/`: `desktop-dropout.jpg`, `phone-390.jpg`, `phone-320.jpg`, and `browser-audit.json`.
+
+Verified journeys:
+
+- Native browser click on Secret's fourth card opened a distinct Abyss tab. Correct target, rel and four-project footer inspected.
+- Enter on Step advances 0.25 s. At the first fix (1 s), worked values show prior 8.127 m, fix 6.652 m, innovation −1.475 m, gain 0.619 and corrected depth 7.214 m.
+- Dropout half-width grows from 0.78 m at 19 s to 3.74 m at 35 s; status shows prediction only and no new fixes.
+- A at R=0.64 versus B at R=4 retains identical rendered fixes and the 60 s timestamp: A RMSE 0.367 m, B 0.371 m. Replay reproduces both.
+- Current and bias summaries inspected; bias demonstrates confidence versus actual error. Numerical default results above include its poor coverage.
+- Playback from 59 s automatically reaches 60 s, disables Step and shows the summary. Keyboard Play/Pause and Reset work; paused time remains unchanged.
+- Actual σ=0.05 matches R=0.0025. ArrowRight changes R to 0.0026 and shows visible focus. Actual-noise changes reset the mission.
+- Learner answer produces correct feedback. No-JS fallback heading appears in `tests/kalman-nojs.html`, whose iframe disallows scripts.
+- Outputs explicitly have `aria-live="off"`; telemetry is not live. Loaded CSSOM contains the valid reduced-motion rule. Final app tab has no captured error/warning console entries.
+
+Unsupported/unperformed checks are not counted as passes: no manual screen-reader speech test, no OS reduced-motion toggle (conditional CSS inspected), no production R2 and no Safari/Firefox testing. Full-page capture on the newly opened tab timed out; viewport captures were recovered by resetting viewport sizing, saved and visually reviewed. Existing Worker was exercised locally against an in-memory bucket, not production.
+
+## Rationale and limitations
+
+The observatory prioritizes fast experiments and failure diagnosis. Actual world and estimator beliefs are visually separated. Pinning creates a reproducible paired experiment without hidden random streams. The restrained mint/orange/violet palette, serif title, custom seafloor and robot establish underwater identity while keeping controls and measured outcomes readable. On phones, the SVG coordinate system changes so the chart is legible rather than letterboxed.
+
+This is a linear depth/vertical-velocity teaching model with known thrust and processed scalar localization depth fixes. It does not model raw sonar ranges/bearings, underwater GPS, DVL, six-degree-of-freedom dynamics, persistent bias estimation, autonomous control, collision physics, or an official RoboSub course. Current and bias intentionally break zero-mean assumptions. The band is a marginal Gaussian depth interval, not guaranteed containment or a planar ellipse. Initial mean equals simulated starting state with nonzero covariance. Dead reckoning integrates the same known commands only. Presets retain tuning; Match matches nominal noise, not current or bias.
+
+Sources are linked in the activity: Welch/Bishop's introduction, Bzarg's visual explanation, RoboNation task descriptions and RoboSub 2026. The primary filter reference was available through search after its direct PDF fetch failed. WCAG 2.2 was consulted. No source prose or external images were copied into the design. Recommendations are design hypotheses, not user-study findings.
+
+## Files and review
+
+New activity files: `kalman/index.html`, `kalman/styles.css`, `kalman/engine.js`, `kalman/app.js`, `kalman/preview.cjs`. New verification: `tests/kalman.test.cjs`, `tests/kalman-nojs.html`, this document and evidence. Updated: `secret/index.html`, `tests/secret-projects.test.cjs`, `README.md`, `work/goal-loop-state.md`. Other projects, shared styles/scripts and `worker.js` were preserved.
+
+Two AGENTS.md cycles: cycle 1 scored **8/10**, identifying phone plot scaling, short slider targets, implicit status outputs and low-noise matching precision. Cycle 2 corrected these, verified mandatory implementation criteria and scored **9/10**. No third revision cycle was needed.
